ial:History/Warana_Raja_Maha_Vihara", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warana_Raja_Maha_Vihara?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Warana_Raja_Maha_Vihara"}}, "extract": "Warana Raja Maha Vihara is an ancient Buddhist temple situated in Thihariya, Gampaha District, Sri Lanka. The temple is located approximately 5\u00a0km (3.1\u00a0mi) away from the Colombo - Kandy highway. Currently this temple has been recognized as an archaeological protected site in Gampaha District by Archaeological department.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Warana Raja Maha Vihara</b> is an ancient Buddhist temple situated in Thihariya, Gampaha District, Sri Lanka. The temple is located approximately 5\u00a0km (3.1\u00a0mi) away from the Colombo - Kandy highway. Currently this temple has been recognized as an archaeological protected site in Gampaha District by Archaeological department.</p>"}